<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ădĭăbēna</span></b> ,
		ae, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ădĭăbēne</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδιαβηνή</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a region in the northern part of ancient
			Assyria</i>, now <i>Botan</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 12,
				13, § 66</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 6, 20
				al.</span></i>— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ădĭăbēnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>pertaining thereto</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Monobazus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 14</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">ib. 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regimen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 2</span></i>
			. —<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ădĭăbēni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>its inhabitants</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 9, 10, §
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ădĭăbēnĭcus</span></b> ,
				<i>a surname of the emperor Severus</i>, <i>as conqueror of Adiabene</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Spart. Sev. 9</span></i>; Sext.
					<i><span class="en">Ruf. 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 903 sq.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
